# Team stats: map, filter, fold, and if

Array combinators take a block. `fold` takes the seed first. `if` is an expression, including inside a method that map calls.

## Schema

```
Team = String/name [Player]/players
Player = String/name Int/score
```

## Construction

```
[:Team
  "Rockets"
  [:Array/Player
    ["Ada" 3]
    ["Bob" 0]
    ["Cy" 5]
  ]
]
```

## Methods

```
Player::label = {
  if (score > 0) { name } else { "bench" }
}

Team::names = { players.map({ p | p.name }) }

Team::labels = { players.map({ p | p.label() }) }

Team::scorers = { players.filter({ p | p.score > 0 }) }

Team::total = { players.fold(0, { acc, p | acc + p.score }) }
```

## Target

```
%terminal

%main
public static function main():Void {
    var team = TeamAssemblage.factory();
    var helper = new WCHNTHelper();
    trace(team.toConstruction(0, helper));
    trace("names");
    trace(helper.arrayToConstruction(team.names(), 0));
    trace("labels");
    trace(helper.arrayToConstruction(team.labels(), 0));
    trace("scorers");
    trace(helper.arrayToConstruction(team.scorers(), 0));
    trace("total");
    trace(team.total());
}
```
